      "html": "<p>Glanidium ribeiroi Haseman, 1911. Family Auchenipteridae. Size: 220 mm SL. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p><p>Type locality: Rio Iguaçú, Porto União da Victoria, Paraná, Brazil.</p><p>Etymology: Glanidium is a diminutive of Greek glanis, meaning catfish, i.e. literally \"small catfish\".</p>"
    },
